1
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:04,800
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:10,610
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,510
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:17,280
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:21,390
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:27,330
We are reaching a crucial moment.

7
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:28,900
Our backs are to the river!

8
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,270
There's no way to escape!

9
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,280
Lay down your lives!

10
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,580
If you don't, we are doomed!

11
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:40,680
If we can survive...

12
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:42,020
...then we'll have won!

13
00:01:02,410 --> 00:01:04,500
Feel no shame about shape

14
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:06,420
Weather changes their phrase

15
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:10,170
Even mother will show you another way

16
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:12,550
So put your glasses on

17
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:14,630
Nothing will be wrong

18
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:16,840
There's no blame. There's no fame

19
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,680
It's up to you

20
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:22,310
The first words should be found

21
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:25,940
Whatever holds you back

22
00:01:26,810 --> 00:01:27,310
I...

23
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:28,440
...can...

24
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,610
I can get it off

25
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:31,610
Tell me what...

26
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:32,610
Tell me what...

27
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:34,440
Tell me what you want

28
00:01:34,570 --> 00:01:35,530
I don't know why...

29
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:36,530
Don't know why...

30
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:38,530
Don't know why you're afraid

31
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,700
Tell me what...

32
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:40,660
Tell me what...

33
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:42,330
Tell me what you'd say

34
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:43,660
I don't know why...

35
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:44,750
Don't know why...

36
00:01:44,830 --> 00:01:45,540
Too late...

37
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,160
It's too late

38
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:56,090
The Conqueror

39
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:32,170
This dry sand is flying everywhere.

40
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:33,340
I can't see anything.

41
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:37,340
Well, it seems certain that our army will win.

42
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:41,550
Did you notice everyone
in the castle has taken off?

43
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:46,060
After all, whoever captures the enemy
leader will get any reward he asks for!

44
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:49,190
So every last one of them
is going after the reward?

45
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:52,060
What rotten luck! Here we are
standing as sentries at a time like this!

46
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:55,150
Hey, what's wrong?

47
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:00,990
The enemy?

48
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,530
Where the hell did they come from?

49
00:03:09,710 --> 00:03:11,210
Charge!

50
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:18,590
First formation, block off the castle gates!

51
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:20,970
Do not allow enemy
messengers to leave the castle!

52
00:03:20,970 --> 00:03:21,630
Got it!

53
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:24,050
The rest of you, carry out the operation!

54
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:24,760
Hurry!

55
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:26,180
There isn't a moment to lose!

56
00:03:32,230 --> 00:03:33,270
Is that...

57
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,610
You go from the right!

58
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:40,190
On the double!

59
00:03:40,610 --> 00:03:42,610
Cover the castle gate and the castle walls!

60
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:44,320
Forget about their command center!

61
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:04,930
Adon to the rescue!

62
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:06,970
It's you...

63
00:04:06,970 --> 00:04:09,060
I'll give you credit for
being a persistent devil.

64
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:14,900
I am well-known as the
indestructible baron, Adon!

65
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:20,110
Everyone inevitably prostrates
themselves before my great vitality!

66
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:24,490
I, Adon, already saw through
all your cheap tricks long ago!

67
00:04:24,950 --> 00:04:28,580
Therefore, I offered
my services as castle guard...

68
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:32,040
...and I waited patiently as you
marched ignorantly toward us.

69
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:33,250
You lie.

70
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:34,830
I do not lie!

71
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:36,460
Everyone, step forward!

72
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:42,840
Behold!

73
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:45,510
The Blue Whale Super Strong Heavy Assault Knights!

74
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:48,890
I purposely left my troops inside
the castle for just such an occasion!

75
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:52,810
Now I am going to have my
revenge for the previous battle!

76
00:04:53,850 --> 00:04:55,020
Listen!

77
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:58,360
Do not allow any of them
to escape with their lives.

78
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,060
Charge!

79
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,530
Let's go!

80
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:04,740
I'll avenge my brother Samson's death!

81
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,240
I give you no quarter!

82
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,300
What's taking them?

83
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:33,220
I have been kept waiting
for Griffith's capture too long!

84
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:34,520
I have a report!

85
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:38,020
A single horseman of great skill
blocks our way to Count Griffith.

86
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,860
Our armed forces cannot
readily get closer to him...

87
00:05:41,190 --> 00:05:43,280
You're all worthless!

88
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:53,370
Who the hell is this man?

89
00:05:53,370 --> 00:05:55,200
Is there no one who can stop him?

90
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:04,460
General Boscone!

91
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:06,010
The general himself?

92
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,090
What?

93
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:45,550
Unbelievable...

94
00:06:45,550 --> 00:06:46,550
Stay out of it!

95
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:48,340
We'll be in trouble if we get
caught up in this fierce battle!

96
00:06:57,980 --> 00:06:58,810
Amazing!

97
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:00,390
That's our big sister all right!

98
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,600
Why is this?

99
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:05,150
Your swordplay is so different than before!

100
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,900
I wasn't feeling too well back then.

101
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,240
The hell you weren't!

102
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,860
Don't make poor excuses...

103
00:07:12,990 --> 00:07:15,120
Wait until I'm finished speaking!

104
00:07:16,030 --> 00:07:18,290
Why don't you keep your
mouth closed for a moment?

105
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:22,790
The enemy has only a small number!

106
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:23,960
Don't let up! Overcome them!

107
00:07:24,330 --> 00:07:27,880
The Band of the Hawk's
future rests on this battle!

108
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:45,810
Thank you, Pippin!

109
00:07:48,030 --> 00:07:49,490
Damn it!

110
00:07:49,490 --> 00:07:52,030
It's just a matter of time
before we're wiped out!

111
00:07:52,030 --> 00:07:53,700
Just look at their numbers!

112
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,990
What are you talking about, Corkus?

113
00:07:55,990 --> 00:07:57,160
Are you saying we should retreat?

114
00:07:58,790 --> 00:08:00,370
I'm not saying that, but...

115
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:05,380
I'd rather go down fighting than run away!

116
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:06,880
Oh no!

117
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,750
Little Rickert has gone insane!

118
00:08:10,510 --> 00:08:11,170
He's right!

119
00:08:12,090 --> 00:08:13,590
I agree with Rickert!

120
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:19,720
My army is utterly overwhelming them!

121
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:21,230
Attack them!

122
00:08:21,230 --> 00:08:23,230
Keep on attacking and overpower them!

123
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:30,690
Boscone, why are you spending
so much time on a mere horseman?

124
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:38,370
Strong!

125
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:40,410
This guy is...

126
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:41,580
...truly strong...

127
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:46,880
I feel closer to death now than when
I was slaughtering a hundred men.

128
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:50,130
I'm going to have to put everything on the line...

129
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:51,630
...or I'll die!

130
00:08:56,090 --> 00:08:57,140
No...

131
00:08:58,260 --> 00:08:59,930
I've been through worse...

132
00:09:08,150 --> 00:09:11,230
This hopelessness is nothing
compared to what I felt then...

133
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,630
How dare you...

134
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:39,470
Only one thing to do now!

135
00:09:42,970 --> 00:09:44,390
I am terribly sorry!

136
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:45,680
What?

137
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:48,770
I beg your pardon for my lack
of courtesy. Please forgive me!

138
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:53,280
After all, I'm just a lowly commander
following orders from the general.

139
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:56,240
Personally, I've never wanted
any sort of grudge against you!

140
00:09:56,650 --> 00:09:57,360
Now, now...

141
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,320
If it's this castle you want, please take it!

142
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,950
I'm the last person who
would stand in your way...

143
00:10:01,950 --> 00:10:04,410
...so please, if you would
kindly spare my life...

144
00:10:05,830 --> 00:10:07,460
What a disgusting man...

145
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:11,500
My clever ruse has put you off guard...

146
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,550
Big sister!

147
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:19,430
Foolish woman!

148
00:10:20,050 --> 00:10:24,310
That was Ressha Jinrai, the secret
art of the crossbow sneak attack...

149
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:26,770
...passed down the Coborlwitz
family for one thousand years!

150
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:30,480
The tip of the arrow was poisoned,
and it will numb your entire body.

151
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:35,690
Your days of sinful deeds
are over, you little bitch!

152
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:37,610
I can't afford...

153
00:10:37,610 --> 00:10:40,320
...to waste my time
playing your foolish games...

154
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:43,330
...any longer!

155
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:58,880
This is bad...

156
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:01,590
My sword was chipped and
cracked in that hundred-man fight...

157
00:11:06,350 --> 00:11:07,890
This is the end...

158
00:11:07,890 --> 00:11:09,350
...for the commander of the Raiders!

159
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:22,200
Here I come!

160
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:25,870
If you put down
your sword like a good girl...

161
00:11:25,870 --> 00:11:29,750
...I might consider letting
you live, as my personal toy.

162
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:32,670
But if you refuse...

163
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:39,010
Take that, and that!

164
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:43,470
Take that and that and that!

165
00:11:44,890 --> 00:11:47,510
Damn it, my body is numb,
and I'm helpless...

166
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:49,020
Big sister!

167
00:12:01,530 --> 00:12:03,490
Well, what are you going to do?

168
00:12:03,490 --> 00:12:05,030
There's nowhere for you to run now...

169
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:11,410
For what you did to my face...

170
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:14,000
Be prepared to lose
at least an arm and a leg!

171
00:12:14,370 --> 00:12:18,550
Then you can tell me whether
or not you want to be my captive...

172
00:12:18,550 --> 00:12:20,710
...and I'll listen at my leisure!

173
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:23,090
Your legs go first!

174
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,220
What?

175
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:34,850
Impossible!

176
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,570
You were a fairly interesting man.

177
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:44,490
Despite being
an irredeemable, revolting bastard!

178
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:54,250
Now!

179
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:55,460
The rest are no match for us!

180
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:56,540
Cut them down!

181
00:13:07,390 --> 00:13:08,260
Now then...

182
00:13:18,730 --> 00:13:20,270
Help the commander!

183
00:13:20,730 --> 00:13:21,650
Get back!

184
00:13:21,650 --> 00:13:22,980
You're no match for him!

185
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,740
Get out of the way!

186
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:46,510
Guts!

187
00:13:46,510 --> 00:13:47,510
Take up that sword!

188
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:18,330
Damn, he managed to do it!

189
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:19,290
Amazing...

190
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:23,710
Utterly worthless!

191
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:24,920
That can't be!

192
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:27,090
The invincible Sir Boscone...

193
00:14:27,090 --> 00:14:28,840
You fools!

194
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,390
Even if the general's been defeated...

195
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:32,260
...our force still has
the upper hand in this battle!

196
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:33,220
How can you falter now?

197
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:36,100
Governor, look at that!

198
00:14:36,470 --> 00:14:37,310
What's that?

199
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:51,490
T-That is...

200
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:53,280
The enemy's flag?

201
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,950
Our castle surrendered?

202
00:14:54,950 --> 00:14:56,240
What's the meaning of this?

203
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,830
Don't you get it yet?

204
00:14:59,370 --> 00:15:01,120
Your commander's dead.

205
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,040
Your castle has fallen!

206
00:15:02,580 --> 00:15:04,340
That can only mean one thing, right?

207
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,300
You've lost this battle!

208
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:07,920
We lost?

209
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:09,470
We really lost?

210
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,800
Everyone, shout!

211
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:13,970
Give a shout of triumph!

212
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:30,030
From now on, we will hunt
the remnants of the enemy.

213
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,990
Only let the enemy pass
if they immediately flee!

214
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:35,780
If they resist, exterminate
every last one of them!

215
00:15:46,090 --> 00:15:47,550
Wait, everyone!

216
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:49,010
I am the commander in chief!

217
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:50,920
I am still alive!

218
00:16:14,490 --> 00:16:15,570
Griffith...

219
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,490
It's been a while, Governor Gennon...

220
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:22,000
Oh, Griffith...

221
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:25,290
I missed you so much.

222
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:27,170
You and I always helped one another.

223
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:29,210
So you'll let me escape
unharmed, won't you?

224
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:33,930
I gave my own soldiers the order that...

225
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,760
...you were not to be
harmed under any circumstances.

226
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:40,220
Of course you understand the
feelings in my heart, don't you?

227
00:16:40,850 --> 00:16:43,850
Not a day passed
that I did not think of you.

228
00:16:44,310 --> 00:16:47,270
We yearned for each other
so passionately that night...

229
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:50,690
You will listen to my plea, won't you?

230
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:55,990
Don't tell me...

231
00:16:56,990 --> 00:16:59,370
...you bear any ill will toward me?

232
00:16:59,990 --> 00:17:02,540
I do not bear any ill feelings at all, Governor.

233
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,580
Oh, then you...

234
00:17:05,080 --> 00:17:08,670
However, it upsets me when you
speak of us yearning for one another...

235
00:17:09,090 --> 00:17:14,220
...for I feel absolutely
nothing for you at all.

236
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:15,930
Neither ill feelings nor otherwise...

237
00:17:15,930 --> 00:17:18,050
What are you talking about, Griffith?

238
00:17:18,510 --> 00:17:23,730
I took advantage of an opportunity, and
you happened to be there at the time.

239
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:26,640
I just picked up a pebble lying in my path...

240
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:29,810
...and it happened to be you.

241
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:33,150
Y-You bastard!

242
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:41,450
At any rate, a chattering
pebble can be quite a nuisance.

243
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:52,210
Unbelievable!

244
00:17:52,210 --> 00:17:53,760
We finally did it!

245
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:55,420
Can you believe it?

246
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:57,970
Are you all right?

247
00:17:57,970 --> 00:17:58,800
Yeah...

248
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,600
I'm feeling a bit better...

249
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,890
Don't worry about me.

250
00:18:02,890 --> 00:18:06,350
You must go and make sure that
no enemies remain within the castle.

251
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:06,980
Right!

252
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:08,060
Hey, get moving.

253
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,100
We've got a job to do!

254
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:09,770
All right!

255
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:39,720
Hey, good job.

256
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:42,800
What's wrong?

257
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:45,140
Just a scratch...

258
00:18:46,430 --> 00:18:48,730
But to tell you the truth...

259
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:51,190
I'd like for you to give me your shoulder.

260
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,490
Amazing...

261
00:19:05,290 --> 00:19:06,330
Hey...

262
00:19:06,330 --> 00:19:07,830
I always feel like this...

263
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:12,750
Whenever I see Griffith
surrounded by his comrades like that...

264
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:16,210
I don't know why, but my
heart becomes filled with sorrow.

265
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:19,050
Because he seems to be so far away...

266
00:19:20,470 --> 00:19:21,840
...beyond my reach.

267
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:30,690
That's not true...

268
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:35,520
Hey, what are you doing?

269
00:19:36,070 --> 00:19:37,070
Let's go.

270
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:41,320
To see your captain.

271
00:19:45,370 --> 00:19:46,280
Yeah...

272
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:58,590
No, it couldn't have been...

273
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:16,060
The time of the Great Eclipse is near.

274
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,900
And the devils will soon descend...

275
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,960
Doldrey Castle has fallen.

276
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:36,330
Thus, this war that we have
waged for so long will be over.

277
00:20:36,330 --> 00:20:38,040
Then Griffith will be free...

278
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:43,130
...to let his political views intrude
into the administration of our kingdom.

279
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:47,180
He is presumptuous enough to do
such things despite his low social rank.

280
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:50,720
His Majesty seems to trust him very much.

281
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:56,020
Because of his recent achievements,
he will attain the position of general.

282
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:57,060
Is that true?

283
00:20:57,060 --> 00:21:00,150
I hear His Majesty will be conferring
the supreme title of White Knights...

284
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:03,280
...on Griffith and the Band of the Hawk,
putting them on equal footing...

285
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:06,070
...with the White Tigers
and the White Dragon Knights!

286
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:07,240
Ridiculous!

287
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:09,620
That will only swell his head even more!

288
00:21:09,950 --> 00:21:16,170
He knows how to survive in battle,
but the noble court is another story.

289
00:21:16,710 --> 00:21:17,710
What is that?

290
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:19,420
Antiaris...

291
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:21,000
...a poison that acts instantaneously...

292
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,670
We shall use this on him...

293
00:21:23,210 --> 00:21:25,550
Are you sure about this?

294
00:21:25,550 --> 00:21:28,470
No matter what, our scheme
must not be traced back to us.

295
00:21:28,470 --> 00:21:31,930
We will not do such a thing ourselves.

296
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:33,220
However...

297
00:21:33,220 --> 00:21:34,560
Do not fear.

298
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,730
Your Majesty!

299
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:44,570
You can leave everything in my hands...

300
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

301
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

302
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

303
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

304
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

305
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

306
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

307
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

308
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

309
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

310
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

